From 6d7bf9efcfc8e1e008fb4be137a28b13861826fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:00:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] agentHost: accept vscode-remote working directories in
 session actions

A window connected to a remote (for example a dev container) dispatches its
workspace folders as vscode-remote: URIs. createSession stored those URIs
verbatim, but resolveSessionWorkingDirectoryAction only accepted file:, so
every dynamic add, remove and replace from such a window was rejected by the
host once the session existed.

Relax the action-path check to the same namespace the create path accepts
(Option A) rather than normalizing to file: at ingress (Option B). Host state
is echoed back to the client unmodified: the protocol client only unwraps
agent-host: URIs on the way in and only wraps file: URIs on the way out, and
the client compares the echoed set against its vscode-remote: workspace
folders with extUri (agentHostSessionListStore and the working-directory
synchronizer). A file: entry would never match those folders, so the session
list would drop the session and the synchronizer would keep re-adding the
folder on every reconcile.

Both paths now share isSupportedWorkingDirectory, and createSession rejects
an unsupported scheme with the same error the action path produces, so the
two cannot drift again. Genuinely unsupported schemes such as untitled: and
https: are still rejected.
